# Session state (machine-local, not shared)
.state/*
!.state/.gitkeep
!.state/workers/
.state/workers/*
!.state/workers/.gitkeep

# Knowledge: operator-private assets are machine-local, not shared (Issue #755).
# - Raw learnings (knowledge/raw/) are machine-local scratch, never committed.
# - The skill-candidate queue's real entries live in the .local.md sibling; the
#   tracked knowledge/skill-candidates.md carries the entry-FORMAT definition
#   only (its entry list is always empty).
# - Operator-private curated notes use the .local.md suffix; the shared
#   operational curated docs (knowledge/curated/*.md without .local) stay tracked.
# See docs/contracts/knowledge-curation-contract.md §3.4.
knowledge/raw/*
!knowledge/raw/.gitkeep
knowledge/skill-candidates.local.md
knowledge/curated/*.local.md

# Project registry: operator-local, generated (Issue #811).
# The tracked artifact is registry/projects.example.md (column schema + spec
# + generic sample rows). The live registry/projects.md carries the
# operator's real roster — customer names, private repo URLs — so it stays
# out of history; /org-start generates it from the template on first run via
# tools/ensure_projects_registry.py.
# Migrating an existing checkout: see docs/operations/registry-projects-migration.md
# (a clean checkout LOSES this file on pull — gitignore does not protect a
# path that was previously tracked).
registry/projects.md
# Migration backups hold the same operator data as the registry itself, so
# they must never be commitable either (the runbook has operators create
# registry/projects.md.bak before pulling the migration).
registry/projects.md.bak*

# Dashboard generated data (replaced by live server)
dashboard/data.json
.state/dashboard.pid

# Dispatcher state (machine-local, not shared)
.dispatcher/.state/

# Curator local config
.curator/.claude/

# Claude Code local config
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.local.override.json
.claude/settings.local.json.bak.*
CLAUDE.local.md

# Dispatcher local config (symmetrical with .curator/.claude/)
.dispatcher/.claude/

# Internal docs (not for public consumption)
docs/internal/
docs/github-issues/

# Python build artifacts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# OS metadata
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Machine-local shell / editor / git dotfiles that land in the repo root
# (Issue #880). These are the operator's environment, never repo content.
# On some WSL setups the harness materialises them at the worktree root as
# /dev/null character devices; while untracked they make a working-tree
# stash with -u abort on a non-regular file — the failure that started the
# "stash saved nothing, the following pop restored another entry" incident.
# Root-anchored (leading /) on purpose: an unanchored pattern would also
# swallow same-named files in subdirectories, and the delegation pattern
# probe (git check-ignore, tools/resolve_worker_layout.py Step 0.7) would
# then misroute a legitimate target into the gitignored sub-mode.
# Deliberately NOT listed: .gitmodules, .mcp.json and .claude/* — this repo
# may legitimately track those (it already tracks .claude/settings.json and
# .claude/skills/), so ignoring them would silently drop a future commit.
# The deny that actually closes the stash accident path lives in
# .hooks/block-dangerous-git.sh; this block only quiets `git status`.
# No trailing slash on /.idea and /.vscode: here they are character devices,
# which git reports as files, so a directory-only pattern would not match.
/.bash_profile
/.bashrc
/.profile
/.zprofile
/.zshrc
/.gitconfig
/.ripgreprc
/.idea
/.vscode

# Environment variables
.env
.env.*
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# M4 (Issue #267): journal.jsonl decommissioned — events table is the SoT.
# Local files lingering from pre-M4 runs are no longer authoritative.
.state/journal.jsonl

# Local Python venv (Secretary main working tree only)
.venv/

# Ad-hoc scratch / log artifacts
tmp/
err.log

# Dispatcher pane snapshot scratch (machine-local)
.dispatcher/panes-snapshot-tmp.json

# codex セルフレビュー用の worker ローカル CODEX_HOME（成果物ではない）
.codex-home/
